I think there's a subtle asymmetry here: a partial-commit failure doesn't increment the counter (the `if (partialCommit)` branch above just logs), but a partial-commit success resets it. So a pattern of full-commit failures interleaved with successful partial commits will keep renewing the retry budget indefinitely, and the counter never trips.

I'd gate the reset on `!partialCommit` so the counter only tracks the codepath that increments it:

```java
doCommit(partialCommit);
if (!partialCommit) {
  consecutiveCommitFailures = 0;
}
```

